---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import ContentSection from '../../components/ContentSection.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — keysprint';
const description =
	'The keysprint privacy policy: no accounts, no cookies, no analytics and no tracking. Only your best score and theme choice are stored, and only in your own browser.';

const updated = '22 October 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
	title={title}
	description={description}
	breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy policy', href: '/privacy-policy/' }]}
>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pb-6 pt-6 sm:px-6">
		<Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Privacy policy', href: '/privacy-policy/' }]} />
	</div>

	<PageHero
		eyebrow="Privacy"
		title="Privacy policy"
		lead="keysprint has no accounts, no cookies, no analytics and no advertising. This page explains exactly what is stored, where it is stored, and why that is the whole list."
	/>

	<ContentSection title="The short version">
		<p>
			keysprint does not collect personal information. It sets no cookies, loads no analytics or
			advertising scripts, and embeds no third party content. The only things stored are your best typing
			score for each test length and your light or dark theme choice, and both are written to your own
			browser's local storage on your own device.
		</p>
		<Callout title="No data leaves your browser" variant="important">
			<p>
				The typing test runs entirely on your machine. The passages are generated locally, your keystrokes
				are measured locally, and your score is calculated locally. Nothing is transmitted to a server,
				because there is no server to transmit it to.
			</p>
		</Callout>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="What is stored, and where">
		<p>
			Two pieces of information are kept, using your browser's local storage. Local storage stays on your
			device and is not sent to any server, not even by the site that wrote it.
		</p>
		<div class="overflow-hidden rounded-card border border-border">
			<table class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm">
				<thead>
					<tr class="bg-surface-2 text-ink">
						<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-semibold">What</th>
						<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-semibold">Why</th>
						<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-semibold">Where</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
					<tr>
						<th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">Your best net speed for each test length and text type</th>
						<td class="px-4 py-2.5">
							So the site can show you a personal best and tell you when you have beaten it.
						</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-2.5">Your browser's local storage</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">Your light or dark theme choice</th>
						<td class="px-4 py-2.5">
							So the site keeps the theme you picked instead of following your system setting every
							time.
						</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-2.5">Your browser's local storage</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<p>
			Both are removed if you clear your browser's site data, and both disappear with the browser profile.
			They are never transmitted, never linked to an account and never visible to anyone else.
		</p>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="What is not collected">
		<ul class="list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 marker:text-ink-subtle">
			<li>
				<strong class="text-ink">No name, email address, phone number or any other identifier.</strong>
				There is no sign-up form anywhere on the site.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-ink">No cookies of any kind.</strong> Not for preferences, not for sessions,
				not for advertising.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-ink">No analytics.</strong> keysprint does not load Google Analytics or any
				other measurement script, and it does not count page views.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-ink">No advertising or ad tracking.</strong> There are no ads, no affiliate
				links and no third party pixels.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-ink">No keystroke logging.</strong> Your typing is measured so that the test
				can score you, and that is all it is used for. It is not recorded, stored or transmitted.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-ink">No third party embeds.</strong> There are no social widgets, no maps, no
				videos and no fonts loaded from another company's servers. The pages use the fonts already on
				your device, which is also why they load quickly.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="The hosting provider">
		<p>
			keysprint is hosted on a free tier of a hosting platform. Like any web host, that provider has to
			process your request in order to send you a page, and it may keep standard technical logs such as
			your IP address, the time of the request and the page requested, for a short period, for security
			and troubleshooting.
		</p>
		<p>
			That handling is done by the host, not by keysprint. keysprint has no access to those logs and does
			not use them for anything. The provider's own privacy documentation explains the details.
		</p>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="Children">
		<p>
			keysprint is a general audience site and is not directed at children. Because it collects no personal
			information from anyone, there is no data for it to hold about a child either.
		</p>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="Your choices">
		<p>
			You can clear the stored data at any time through your browser's settings, and clearing your
			browsing data removes the best scores and the theme preference along with everything else. There is
			nothing else to delete, because there is nothing else.
		</p>
		<p>
			If you have a question about anything on this page, the
			<a href="/contact/" class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-ink">contact page</a> explains how
			to reach the person behind the site.
		</p>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="Changes to this policy">
		<p>
			If this policy changes, the page will be updated and the date at the top will change with it. There
			is no list to sign up for and no notification to send, because the site does not collect an address
			to send one to.
		</p>
		<p class="text-sm text-ink-subtle">Last updated: {updated}.</p>
	</ContentSection>
</BaseLayout>
